// Duplicate dict keys (warning grade): two entries of one dict literal
// with the same literal key — the code is legal but the author almost
// certainly meant a different key. The compile proceeds and the program
// prints the surviving value. Exit code 0 = exact.
void main() {
    var d = {"a": 1, "a": 2, "b": 3};
    printline(d["a"]);
    printline(d["b"]);
}
